r thoughts on this tv show  and about fall  what did you like about metres gambit  that is our experience  um  first of all uh i i love the  the the tv show queen's queen's gambit i  thought the chess part was  really really well made with lots of  little  nuggets about chess and chess history  and game games that also i hadn't seen  before  as well as being a very  um interesting story that was well acted  i would say here um  i'm loving the fact that  the  hotel the resort they're innovating  thinking of something new i know that  spain is a country that has a great  tradition in chess a lot of people  love the game and in that sense it's um  it's a perfect combination oh thank you  how do you imagine the perfect place to  play chess  i would say um  perfect place to to play chess is  very close to to to here it's  a beautiful  beautiful garden with  no distractions  um what advice would you give to a  person who is starting  the art of chess yeah  i would say  for me personally what  always was the driver for me in chess is  that i found it to be fun and to be  interesting  and that has lasted to me  uh to to this day  so  um when you start out in chess be a  little bit patient because it doesn't  come out  it you don't you're not going to get  everything immediately  but after after that  um yeah do what is interesting do what  it do what is fun if it's just  wonderful because i think it's it's uh  it's a it's a beautiful transcendent  game but if it's something else  sure  in your case do you remember at what age  you discovered chess and how was their  way towards your your vocation and  professional career  i would say that i started um playing  chess i started learning the moves when  i was about  five and a half years old  uh and i kind of liked the game but i  didn't have the  the patience to like sit down and try  and study it to learn more so  i actually i would say that i started  learning more about chess when i was  eight i became really  interested first of all my first goal  was to beat my older sister  and after that  i just fell in love with with the game  and  i would always study study on my own and  i think it's been only one way since  and based on your own experience which  are the benefits of this sport for those  who practice it  i would say that  two  two things have been important for me  chess teaches you to think  analytically  and to be to be patient but i think it  also teaches you to make decisions under  pressure  and  in chess you're constantly under  pressure from  from time factors both on the board and  also on the clock and this you will find  to be  um  important in any  in any profession that you have to make  well calculated but sometimes also quick  uh decisions under under pressure and  this you learn perfectly from  and in which way do you expect this  final will be different from the last  championship in 2018 and 2020.  sorry 2016 16. um personally i'm hoping  that this time there will be  maybe fewer draws than there have been  in the last few  times  because  basically i have not led a world  championship match in  a classical chess since 2014 so the last  two matches have been really close i'm  really hoping that there will be a  little bit more uh back and forth  rather than a drawn out battle that it's  it's been the last few times so that is  my my hope and also my belief so  thank you very much  magnus that that was it so thank you  thank you  [Music]  [Music]  you

